[TEXT] ## Phase 2 → Phase 3 — Real symptoms confirmed

Both direct-IP probes return hard failures:
- **pc2 → 195.11.14.2**: `"Network is unreachable"` — an immediate, LOCAL routing-table miss on pc2 (no route to the partner network, not even a timeout)
- **pc1 → 200.1.1.2**: 10 s timeout — pc1 can send but receives no reply (consistent with pc2 having no return path)

Both symptoms are explained by a single fault on pc2: a missing route to the partner network means pc2 cannot send packets outbound AND cannot send ICMP replies back to pc1.

**Active lead:** pc2 has no usable route for 195.11.14.0/24 — per-host addressing/routing anomaly on pc2 after maintenance.

**Fault family:** `host-ip-skill` — per-host routing/gateway misconfiguration on pc2.
